# packages/web build context (issue #3938).
#
# The `builder` stage does a bare `COPY . .` after `npm ci`, so anything here
# reaches the build unless excluded. `npm ci` already produces a fresh,
# linux-target node_modules inside the image from the committed
# package-lock.json — copying the host's node_modules over that is never
# correct: at best it's dead weight, at worst (host-platform native binaries
# like esbuild, or a worktree's node_modules symlink) it silently produces a
# build for the wrong platform, or makes the `COPY` itself fail outright
# ("cannot replace to directory .../app/node_modules with file").
#
# .env is local-only and never read at build time (Vite bakes in build-time
# env via --build-arg / compose env, not a copied .env file) — shipping it
# into the builder stage risks leaking whatever secrets a developer has in
# their local file, even though it never reaches the final nginx stage today.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Build output / caches — never inputs to this Dockerfile, only outputs of it
# or of local `npm run` scripts.
dist
**/dist
coverage
**/coverage
playwright-report
**/playwright-report
test-results
**/test-results
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
*.log
**/*.log

# Editor / OS cruft
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
.idea
**/.idea
.vscode
**/.vscode
